    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T06:57:54Z",
    "body": "Maintainer decision (owner's standing word 2026-11-22: choose recommended while he sleeps).\n\nThe test of the agent of mkinney gives the answer: a hole that is tilted from the tool axis is not recognized as a Z hole. The circle fit refuses the wall (`FIT_TOL`), and a mutation of `FIT_TOL` makes the pin fail. So no wrong cut is possible here; the hypothesis of this issue is false.\n\n- Option 1 (taken, recommended): keep the test as a pin, as this issue asks. PR #3651 takes the branch `mkinney:issue/3554-tilted-hole-pin` (commit `418e88034`) as it is. An independent run and a read follow; the merge closes this issue.\n- Option 2 (dropped): close with no pin.\n\nA tilted hole is dropped with no named message. That is an enhancement and gets its own issue if a user asks for it.\n",
